  "proof": [
    "Native Linux AMD64/amd64_sysv is little-endian; admitted fresh ordinary variant is fully zeroed before its sole tag width change.",
    "At most8 declared cases gives a tag <=7; zero-extended storel writes the same low4bytes as storew and zeroes already-zero padding4..7; payload offset8 and size>=16 prevent payload/neighbor overlap.",
    "Active payload is exact builtin i64 or compiler-created float identity with no fields/management/runtime identity/move-only/callback and a copyable, uncounted, nonunique RC shape. User domains/bool/empty/niche/boxed/fielded/unsupported layouts fall back.",
    "Full zero, internal journal, source address, destination address, region mark, ordinary scalar load/store, result publication, error trace and finish are unchanged and ordered identically. No callback, allocation, tag/IEEE/overflow/bounds/root/COW check is changed.",
    "GC, borrowed-body and legacy-sharing lowering bypass the existing RC aggregate entry. RC counting has only the same physical-store width change and retains its journal/glue/events.",
    "Real native.Catalog field metadata assigns every case payload at shared payload_offset8; exactly one matching active field and <=8 bounded physical fields are required."
